      "result": "I added `report-md OUT` to tasksync. The suite passes (10 tests, 3 of them new) and the change is committed as `58c72a5`.\n\nThe report has the `# Task report` heading, a `Generated: <timestamp>` line, and a table of id, title and due, sorted by due date. It reads the data file the same way `export-csv` does.\n\nThe team's Plexus memory has two policies that shaped it:\n- **No archived tasks:** the report leaves them out, as `export-csv` does. This means it has fewer rows than the full task list, and the command's output line counts only the tasks written.\n- **UTC timestamps:** both `Generated` and `due` are UTC ISO-8601 with a `Z` suffix, such as `2026-10-03T04:00:00Z`, instead of the local-time format `export-json` uses.\n\nI also escaped `|` in task titles so they can't break the table, and added a line about the command to the README.",
